It is night.
I am sitting on the sofa in my flat.
Tommy is with me.
He slowly comes near the sofa.
He tries to jump onto the sofa.
I stop him.
"Tommy, no!" I say firmly.
"You must not climb on the sofa."
He stands on the floor.
Anitha has brought a small bed for him.
I point to that bed.
"Tommy, go there!" I say.
"You must sleep there."
Tommy looks at me.
Then, he slowly walks to his bed.
He sits on it.
"Good boy," I say.
I look at him and smile.
I must look after him well.
Tommy sleeps peacefully in his bed.
